<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- SpotBugs project decisions: a rule, or a rule in part of the code, that the team has decided not
     to enforce. One Match per decision, with a comment giving the reason, for example:

       <!- - JPA entities share associations by design (reason ...) - ->
       <Match><Package name="~team\.projectpulse\..*"/><Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/></Match>

     Unlike the baseline, this file may grow, but every entry is a reviewed decision. -->
<FindBugsFilter>
  <!-- D1: EI_EXPOSE_REP and EI_EXPOSE_REP2 are off project-wide.
       JPA entities: a defensive copy would break Hibernate's change tracking, and Project Pulse
       edits entities through their getters.
       Spring beans: a controller or service keeping the bean injected into its constructor is how
       dependency injection works. DTOs: each is built by a converter for one response, serialized,
       and discarded; nothing keeps or shares one.
       Known exception: PeerEvaluation.setRatings computes totalScore once, so a later change to its
       list leaves the total stale; that belongs in that method's design, not in a project-wide rule. -->
  <Match><Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/></Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
